## Agora Agent Configuration Example
## Copy this file to .env and adjust settings as needed

## === LLM Configuration ===

## Azure OpenAI Configuration (TRAPI)
## For Microsoft internal TRAPI endpoints
# AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT="https://trapi.research.microsoft.com/gcr/shared"
# AOAI_SCOPE="api://trapi/.default"
# API_VERSION="2025-04-01-preview"

## Azure Foundry Configuration
## Required for Azure Foundry and DeepResearch
# AZURE_AI_FOUNDRY_ENDPOINT="https://agora-research-resource.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/agora-research"
# DEEP_RESEARCH_MODEL_DEPLOYMENT_NAME="o3-deep-research"
# MODEL_DEPLOYMENT_NAME="gpt-4o"
# BING_RESOURCE_NAME="agorabing"
# BING_GROUNDING_CONNECTION_ID="/subscriptions/7be6291d-d314-4fb5-8377-b89b8b116529/resourceGroups/agora-foundry-rg/providers/Microsoft.CognitiveServices/accounts/agora-research-resource/projects/agora-research/connections/agorabing"

## === Authentication Configuration ===

## Auth mode: The system supports two authentication modes:
##   1. Entra ID (default) - uses Azure CLI or Managed Identity tokens
##   2. API Key - uses service-specific API keys (for OSS/non-Entra environments)
##
## When API key env vars (e.g., AZURE_SEARCH_API_KEY) are set, key-based auth
## is used automatically for the corresponding service. Otherwise, Entra ID
## is used via the ChainedTokenCredential (CLI → Managed Identity).

## Authentication uses ChainedTokenCredential that tries methods in order:
## 1. AzureCliCredential (for local development with `az login`)
## 2. ManagedIdentityCredential (for Azure resources with managed identity)

## Optional: Specify resource and client ID for managed identity
# DEFAULT_IDENTITY_RESOURCE_ID="/subscriptions/7be6291d-d314-4fb5-8377-b89b8b116529/resourceGroups/agora-rg/providers/Microsoft.ManagedIdentity/userAssignedIdentities/agora-identity"
# DEFAULT_IDENTITY_CLIENT_ID="3b39d9dc-61ad-432f-b387-d6914d5f81e9"

## --- API Key Authentication (for OSS / non-Entra environments) ---
## Set these to use key-based auth instead of Entra ID.
## When set, the corresponding service will use the API key automatically.

## Azure AI Search query or admin key
# AZURE_SEARCH_API_KEY="your-search-api-key"

## Azure Storage connection string (for blob/table access without Entra)
# AZURE_STORAGE_CONNECTION_STRING="DefaultEndpointsProtocol=https;AccountName=...;AccountKey=...;EndpointSuffix=core.windows.net"

## Authentication scope for MCP servers
# MCP_SERVER_SCOPE="api://12c90937-013c-468e-93cf-eb8083d69ca7/.default"

## === MCP Code Execution Server Configuration ===

## Entra ID application configuration for MCP code execution servers
## Required for token validation in deployed environments.

## Application (client) ID of the MCP server app registration
# ENTRA_CLIENT_ID="12c90937-013c-468e-93cf-eb8083d69ca7"

## Azure AD tenant ID
# ENTRA_TENANT_ID="72f988bf-86f1-41af-91ab-2d7cd011db47"

## Managed Identity (Azure Container Apps)
## Set AZURE_CLIENT_ID to the client ID of a user-assigned managed identity.
# AZURE_CLIENT_ID="your-user-assigned-managed-identity-client-id"

## === DataLake Artifact Registry Configuration ===

## Azure AI Search resource name and endpoint for artifact registry
# DATA_LAKE_SEARCH_NAME="agora-ai-search"
# DATA_LAKE_SEARCH_ENDPOINT="https://agora-ai-search.search.windows.net"

## DataLake artifact registry index name in Azure AI Search
## Default: artifact-registry
# DATA_LAKE_CATALOG_INDEX_NAME="artifact-registry"

## Datalake blob details index name in Azure AI Search
## Default: blob-details
# DATA_LAKE_BLOB_DETAILS_INDEX="blob-details"

## Azure OpenAI model to be used for vectorization in artifact registry
# DATA_LAKE_VECTORIZER_ENDPOINT="https://agora-research-resource.cognitiveservices.azure.com/openai/deployments/text-embedding-3-large/embeddings?api-version=2023-05-15"
# DATA_LAKE_VECTORIZER_DEPLOYMENT="text-embedding-3-large"

## === Tool Search Configuration ===

## Azure AI Search-based tool discovery (alternative to BM25).
# TOOL_SEARCH_ENDPOINT="https://agora-ai-search.search.windows.net"

## Azure OpenAI model to be used for vectorization of tool descriptions
# TOOL_SEARCH_VECTORIZER_ENDPOINT="https://agora-research-resource.cognitiveservices.azure.com/openai/deployments/text-embedding-3-large/embeddings?api-version=2023-05-15"
# TOOL_SEARCH_VECTORIZER_DEPLOYMENT="text-embedding-3-large"

## === Tool-Learning Vignettes Configuration ===

## The VignetteRunMiddleware and VignetteFunctionMiddleware use these settings
## to persist and retrieve anti-pattern vignettes.  Vignettes are written to
## Azure Table Storage when tool-call repairs succeed, and retrieved from
## Azure AI Search to inject guardrails before inference.
## Authentication uses the shared credential from core.auth (CLI → Managed Identity).
## Leave all unset to disable the middleware entirely.

## Azure Table Storage endpoint for vignette persistence
# TOOL_LEARNING_TABLE_ENDPOINT="https://grid0eastus2.table.core.windows.net/"

## Table name for vignette entities (default: ToolVignettes)
# TOOL_LEARNING_TABLE_NAME="ToolVignettes"

## Azure AI Search endpoint for vignette retrieval (hybrid keyword + vector)
# TOOL_LEARNING_SEARCH_ENDPOINT="https://agora-ai-search.search.windows.net"

## Azure AI Search index name (default: tool-vignettes)
# TOOL_LEARNING_SEARCH_INDEX="tool-vignettes"

## Maximum number of vignettes to retrieve per tool (default: 5)
# TOOL_LEARNING_TOP_K="5"

## Minimum confidence threshold for retrieved vignettes (default: 0.0)
# TOOL_LEARNING_MIN_CONFIDENCE="0.0"
